{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 11, :comments ["<b>Why do You turn back</b> — as in <i>תשיב אחור ימינו</i> (You turn back Your right hand). Your left hand — it is as though He mentioned two of Your hands, by way of parable. And the truth is: <i>תכלה מקרב השוכן שם</i> (You destroy from the midst of the one who dwells there), which is Your enemies."], :book :psalms, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 74, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [["Ibn Ezra on Psalms -- Daat" "http://www.daat.ac.il/he-il/tanach/parshanut_hamikra/full-text/eben-ezra/tehilim"] ["Wikisource Mikraot Gedolot" "http://en.wikisource.org/wiki/Mikraot_Gedolot/"] ["Tanakh, Venice, 1617-1619" "https://dlib.rsl.ru/viewer/01007514045#?page=4"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T19:34:26.587083831Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}